                <pb facs="0287" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.6363/444: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-05T15:00:00-04:00">August 5, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Embassy’s 150, July 29, 10 a.m. Embassy is informed that the private oil
                    companies have applied for enrollment on register <pb facs="0288" n="189"
                        xml:id="pg189"/> mentioned in article 4 of executive decree and are now
                    waiting to see what action YPF takes regarding their importation requests.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
